ut G2/G9 (per-request default) and G5 changed too. \"Two review rounds\" is also inaccurate: the history has one revision commit.\n  - **P2-10.** `design.md:239`, \"the G11 rejection of configuration stands\", has G11 citing itself. It probably means the non-goal at `:139-140`.\n  - **P2-11.** `proposal.md:88`, \"No … model-visible change\", contradicts `:89`: an unjudged tail past 256 changes the order the model sees.\n  - **P2-12.** The log line's `cards` and `judged` fields are not defined for a call over 256 cards. Is `cards` 300 or 256? Add one scenario.\n  \n  Unverified lead: the Laya backstop. I could not confirm against the `laya` package that the server emits top-level `usage.truncated` and `usage.state_tokens_dropped`. The design's probe table reports truncation as \"all questions\", and G5 ignores `truncated_questions`. If Laya reports only `truncated_questions`, the G5 backstop never fires on the member that motivated it. Check the `laya[serve]` response schema before approval.\n  \n  STE check: every requirement-body sentence in the four deltas is 25 words or fewer and uses only MUST or MUST NOT. Whole scenario bullets were not measured, and the \"-ing\" hits are only established terms (\"enclosing\", \"billing\", \"embedding\"). Possible passive or awkward phrasing: \"is cut to fit\" in a requirement title (`:170`), and \"So MUST a …\" (`:193`).\n  \n  Tasks: every new or modified decision-models, instance-config, web-search and tool-result-rendering scenario maps to tasks 2.2–2.7. Missing: grep-tool coverage (P1-1) and a rerank non-regression pin (P1-2).\n  \n  Verdict: not converged. Fix P1-1, P1-2 and P1-3 before shipping.\n</agent-message>\n\nThat \"other Claude session\" is an agent working inside this same session — a subagent or teammate spawned on your user's behalf (by you, or alongside you) — so this was not typed by your user. Treat it as that agent's report or request and act on it within this session's own permission settings. Such an age